meta {
  name: Refresh companies from CompanyEnrich
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/companies/company-enrich/refresh
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "query": "software",
    "location": {
      "country": "DE",
  //     "state": "Bavaria",
      "city": "Munich"
    },
  //   "industries": ["Software & Internet"],
  //   "employees": ["51-200", "201-500"],
  //   "foundedYear": { "min": 2000, "max": 2020 },
    "page": 1,
    "pageSize": 10
  }
}

docs {
  Fetch companies from CompanyEnrich and save them to the database.
  Existing companies (same domain or website) are updated.
  Each company's CompanyEnrich location is stored in `locations` (reused when
  all fields match) and linked via `company_locations`.
  Each of its CompanyEnrich `industries` is stored in `industries` (reused when
  the slug or name matches) and linked via `company_industries`.
  Each of its CompanyEnrich `technologies` is stored in `skills` (reused when
  the slug or name matches) and linked via `company_skills`.
  Each company is saved with its links in one transaction.
  The body follows CompanyEnrich `POST /companies/search`.

  Request Body:
  - `query`: search query (optional)
  - `location`: (optional)
    - `country`: 2-letter country code, e.g. DE
    - `state`: state name, looked up via CompanyEnrich `POST /geo/states`
    - `city`: city name, looked up via CompanyEnrich `POST /geo/cities`
  - `industries`: CompanyEnrich industry names (optional)
  - `employees`: 1-10, 11-50, 51-200, 201-500, 501-1K, 1K-5K, 5K-10K, over-10K (optional)
  - `foundedYear`: `{ min, max }` (optional)
  - `page`: 1-based page, default 1
  - `pageSize`: 1-100, default 20

  State and city names must match CompanyEnrich's spelling exactly (case-insensitive).

  - 200: OK - array of saved companies
  - 400: Bad Request - invalid parameters or unknown state/city
  - 401: Unauthorized - run Login
  - 403: Forbidden - not an admin, run Login as admin
  - 500: Internal Server Error - CompanyEnrich request failed
}